      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.22,
      "end_seconds": 7.16,
      "duration_seconds": 5.94,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, hello, doctor. May I come in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.96,
      "end_seconds": 13.33,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "Yes, come in and and sit down. What brings you here today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.3,
      "end_seconds": 22.54,
      "duration_seconds": 7.24,
      "text": "Doctor, it's some soreness from the stitches. It's getting on my nerves now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.69,
      "end_seconds": 26.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "time for your numbers, if that's okay"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.9,
      "end_seconds": 36.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "That's it, just a a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.89,
      "end_seconds": 64.28,
      "duration_seconds": 16.39,
      "text": "Okay: weight 92 kilos, temperature 36.6, height 176 centimetres. And And pulse is 74 beats a minute, oxygen saturation is 98 percent, pressure 124 over 70. Alright, has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.34,
      "end_seconds": 77.0,
      "duration_seconds": 10.66,
      "text": "Hm. It was either the end of last month or earlier than that. I couldn't tell you the date."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.68,
      "end_seconds": 81.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "How much trouble does it give you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.66,
      "end_seconds": 85.24,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "Moderate, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.08,
      "end_seconds": 89.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Any other symptoms with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.98,
      "end_seconds": 108.3,
      "duration_seconds": 17.32,
      "text": "Erm, it usually comes with bleeding that is tailing off. The bleeding that is tailing off? That's been for three days. I'd been feeling tired after the birth, but that went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.15,
      "end_seconds": 114.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "Any leg swelling, fever or thoughts of harming the baby?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.42,
      "end_seconds": 119.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "No, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.75,
      "end_seconds": 123.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Is your chest okay generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.81,
      "end_seconds": 125.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.12,
      "end_seconds": 128.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "does your family have any medical conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.92,
      "end_seconds": 139.65,
      "duration_seconds": 8.73,
      "text": "My uncle has high cholesterol. Sorry, what was I saying, my daughter has type 1 diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.81,
      "end_seconds": 145.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.05,
      "end_seconds": 162.5,
      "duration_seconds": 16.45,
      "text": "It's fluoxetine, 20 milligrams, every morning. Uh, though honestly, some days I forget to take it. Propranolol. I take it 40 milligrams, twice a day. Uh, I take bisoprolol, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.14,
      "end_seconds": 165.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "How much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.65,
      "end_seconds": 171.95,
      "duration_seconds": 6.3,
      "text": "It's 2.5 milligrams. Paracetamol. I take it 1 gram, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.72,
      "end_seconds": 192.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "What operations have you had, if any?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.5,
      "end_seconds": 200.54,
      "duration_seconds": 6.04,
      "text": "Right, yes, I had my septum straightened, in my thirties."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.07,
      "end_seconds": 206.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.69,
      "end_seconds": 213.85,
      "duration_seconds": 6.16,
      "text": "I've got depression i've had migraines, yes i have an irregular heartbeat"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.68,
      "end_seconds": 220.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "Okay, I can see depression in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.18,
      "end_seconds": 239.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Do you work outside the home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 243.14,
      "end_seconds": 247.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.37,
      "end_seconds": 249.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.95,
      "end_seconds": 254.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.97,
      "end_seconds": 257.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "How active are you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.8,
      "end_seconds": 262.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "I hardly move around during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.79,
      "end_seconds": 273.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 275.28,
      "end_seconds": 276.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "No known allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.41,
      "end_seconds": 281.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "let's move on to the examination"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.4,
      "end_seconds": 285.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "so, tell me if that's sore"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.96,
      "end_seconds": 304.6,
      "duration_seconds": 6.64,
      "text": "The womb has gone down well and the stitches are healing, with no redness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.6,
      "end_seconds": 325.22,
      "duration_seconds": 16.62,
      "text": "You can sit up now. Okay, so my impression is this: My working impression is a normal postnatal recovery. I'd also keep the baby blues in mind. Let's get a blood count, for postnatal tiredness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 325.73,
      "end_seconds": 328.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "the earliest is Thursday, 10 am"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.76,
      "end_seconds": 341.52,
      "duration_seconds": 7.76,
      "text": "Rest when the baby sleeps and ask for help; contraception can be discussed at six weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 341.79,
      "end_seconds": 356.85,
      "duration_seconds": 15.06,
      "text": "Hm, okay. If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department. I'll want another look in four weeks. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 361.06,
      "end_seconds": 366.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
